        "code": "def priority(item: float, bins: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Return one priority for each feasible bin.\n\n    ``bins`` contains remaining capacities after filtering bins that cannot\n    hold ``item``.  The evaluator selects the first maximum priority and\n    opens a new bin when the array is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Best-fit-like baseline: prefer the bin with the smallest remaining\n    # capacity after placing the item, but mildly break ties toward bins\n    # whose post-placement residual is closer to zero in a ratio sense.\n    residual = bins - item\n    return -residual - 0.001 * (residual * residual)",
